wearing a prison jumpsuit?

47
00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.577
Is Scotland exporting insanity

48
00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.037
and doesn't Florida
have a surplus?

49
00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.872
That jumpsuit isn't
from a normal prison.

50
00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.165
It's from The Triangle.

51
00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:05.876
America's secret
maximum security prison

52
00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.878
at the heart
of the Bermuda Triangle.

53
00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.088
We have a paranormal Guantanamo?

54
00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:12.382
Well. we can't put a ghost
in a regular prison. Banks.

55
00:02:12.466 --> 00:02:13.526
Because they would love it.

56
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.861
Because they'd walk
through the walls.

57
00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:15.987
Unless they were ghost walls.

58
00:02:16.011 --> 00:02:17.405
Oh. and you don't think
they'd love that?

59
00:02:17.429 --> 00:02:19.640
The Triangle is supposed
to be a sealed box.

60
00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:21.475
But pointier.
With less sides.

61
00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:23.644
This is the fourth escape
in three years.

62
00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:25.353
Hm.
It's almost like a sealed.

63
00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:27.439
pointy box full of bad stuff
eventually erupts.

64
00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:28.541
They should invent
a name for that.

65
00:02:28.565 --> 00:02:29.483
Lava pyramid.

66
00:02:29.566 --> 00:02:31.234
Our monster prison
isn't leaking monsters

67
00:02:31.318 --> 00:02:33.153
because of chaos theory.
dorkatron.

68
00:02:33.236 --> 00:02:35.656
All of these escapees
have happened under one warden.

69
00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:37.574
And look at this...
every single escapee

70
00:02:37.658 --> 00:02:40.077
was registered in
the prison logs as deceased

71
00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.162
before they could
have possibly escaped.

72
00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:43.598
They're getting help
from the inside.

73
00:02:43.622 --> 00:02:44.539
Corrupt guards?

74
00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:46.100
Or you think it goes
all the way up to the warden?

75
00:02:46.124 --> 00:02:47.250
I don't get paid to think.

76
00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:50.128
I mean. I do a little.
but I get results through action.

77
00:02:50.212 --> 00:02:52.673
It's time the Triangle
got a surprise inspection.

78
00:02:52.756 --> 00:02:55.466
Marine style.
White gloves and armored boots.

79
00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.928
With fine-toothed combs
on the toes of the boots.

80
00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.721
3D-printed to fit
the insides of asses.

81
00:02:59.805 --> 00:03:01.473
I am so pumped for this.

82
00:03:01.556 --> 00:03:03.600
Good. because you're going in
undercover.

83
00:03:03.684 --> 00:03:05.560
-As an inmate.
-Wait. wha... sir?

84
00:03:05.644 --> 00:03:07.497
It does makes sense to go in
from the top and the bottom.

85
00:03:07.521 --> 00:03:08.831
We'd never know
which guards are corrupt

86
00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.941
by asking a warden
that's complicit or oblivious.

87
00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.402
You're a man I can trust.
and. as a half-leprechaun.

88
00:03:13.485 --> 00:03:15.112
you'd be fast-tracked
to the Triangle.

89
00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:18.240
I'm a man you can trust because
I hate that I'm half-leprechaun.

90
00:03:18.323 --> 00:03:19.741
I literally never lie.

91
00:03:19.825 --> 00:03:21.284
I can't pretend
to be a criminal.

92
00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:23.036
Who says you'd be pretending.
you fancy.

93
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.800
gold-sucking. rainbow-loving
piece of shit?

94
00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.331
-Sir.
-No. No.

95
00:03:26.415 --> 00:03:27.624
I know what you're doing.

96
00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:29.501
I stole yer lucky charms.
me boy!

97
00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:30.711
What... what is happening?

98
00:03:30.794 --> 00:03:32.313
He's trying to goad me
into assaulting him

99
00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:34.756
by saying lepre-phobic shit.
which makes zero sense

100
00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:37.384
because I'm already ashamed
of my paranormal ethnicity.

101
00:03:37.466 --> 00:03:38.760
You love your mother.

102
00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:46.560
Damn! Can't believe I got
put next to the guy

103
00:03:46.643 --> 00:03:48.204
who assaulted the President
with a stapler.

104
00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.646
What'd they get you for?

105
00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.370
Eh. lured some schoolgirls
into the woods.

106
00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:52.482
made 'em stab each other.

107
00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:53.984
But they got me on tax evasion.

108
00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.694
Sorry. I-I gotta sit down.

109
00:04:01.783 --> 00:04:03.368
Actually kind of excited. sir.

110
00:04:03.452 --> 00:04:04.703
It's my first recon mission.

111
00:04:04.786 --> 00:04:06.146
And based on our
recent field work.

112
00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:08.457
I've adopted a more versatile
system of safety protocols.

113
00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.417
Don't nerf yourself
for my sake. Banks.

114
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.253
I do dangerous work. and I need
dangerous people on my team.

115
00:04:14.171 --> 00:04:15.005
Whew!

116
00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:18.091
Faster than a velociraptor.
but still slower than a baby yeti.

117
00:04:18.175 --> 00:04:20.177
Also. how dangerous do you
really want your people?

118
00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:22.929
Our country has a secret
detention center for freaks.

119
00:04:23.013 --> 00:04:25.390
and your only problem
is that sometimes they get out.

120
00:04:25.474 --> 00:04:26.794
It's not a prison
for quirky X-Men

121
00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.477
and sexy scissorhands. Banks.

122
00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.937
It's the only place capable
of housing literal monsters

123
00:04:31.021 --> 00:04:32.397
that commit actual crimes.

124
00:04:32.481 --> 00:04:35.066
So I should be a dangerous freak
but never a criminal monster.

125
00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.611
-And the difference is?
-You're on my team.

126
00:04:37.694 --> 00:04:38.570
Mr. President!

127
00:04:38.653 --> 00:04:40.363
We're entering the Triangle's
outer fringe!

128
00:04:40.447 --> 00:04:42.282
This is as far
as Air Force One can go.

129
00:04:42.365 --> 00:04:43.700
What?
But we're still in the air.

130
00:04:43.784 --> 00:04:45.076
Yep.
Time to change planes.

131
00:04:45.159 --> 00:04:46.828
Deploying umbilical!

132
00:04:48.371 --> 00:04:50.457
Secured and ready
for passengers!

133
00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:56.171
Hello. Mister President!

134
00:04:56.254 --> 00:04:57.506
Welcome aboard!

135
00:04:57.589 --> 00:04:58.840
Thanks for the assist. Amelia.

136
00:04:58.924 --> 00:05:00.884
Wait. Amelia?
As in Earhart?

137
00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:03.428
-The one and only. dollface.
-Ooh!

138
00:05:03.512 --> 00:05:06.056
She's the only pilot that can
navigate the Bermuda Triangle.

139
00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.600
FDR's people found her here
flying in circles.

140
00:05:08.683 --> 00:05:10.560
so they put her in charge
of Triangle transit.

141
00:05:10.644 --> 00:05:12.729
Classic FDR.
just giving out jobs.

142
00:05:12.813 --> 00:05:14.773
Then Truman gave me
these babies!

143
00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:19.860
Yes!

144
00:05:28.954 --> 00:05:30.413
So... she can never land?

145
00:05:30.497 --> 00:05:32.374
Wouldn't want to. kid!
Love flying.

146
00:05:32.457 --> 00:05:34.334
Landing?
That's for cars!

147
00:05:35.627 --> 00:05:36.837
-Uhh...
-We're here!

148
00:05:39.548 --> 00:05:41.424
Here. put this on.
We parachute from here.

149
00:05:41.508 --> 00:05:43.552
Okay. fun. Huge fan.

150
00:05:43.635 --> 00:05:45.887
Thank you for all
you've done for Americans.

151
00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:47.722
And women.
And lesbians.

152
00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:49.015
You're welcome!

153
00:05:49.099 --> 00:05:51.101
Wait. people are
still doing labels?

154
00:05:51.183 --> 00:05:52.936
Whoo-hoo!

155
00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.523
Alright. Banks. no matter
what this guy says or does.

156
00:05:56.606 --> 00:05:58.125
remember we're not here
to make friends.

157
00:05:58.149 --> 00:06:00.735
Mister President.
Warden Ken Jeffries.

158
00:06:00.819 --> 00:06:02.112
Save the pleasantries. Warden.

159
00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.572
I'm here for a full inspection.

160
00:06:03.655 --> 00:06:04.948
Loud and clear. sir.

161
00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:06.342
That's how we did it
in the Marines.

162
00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.409
You're a Marine?

163
00:06:07.492 --> 00:06:09.035
Three-Eight. Camp Lawson.
Okinawa.

164
00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:10.203
-Oo-rah!
-Oo-rah!

165
00:06:10.287 --> 00:06:11.162
-Oo-rah!
-Oo-rah!

166
00:06:11.246 --> 00:06:12.080
-Oo-rah!
-Oo-rah!

167
00:06:12.163 --> 00:06:12.998
-Oo-rah!
-Yeah!

168
00:06:13.081 --> 00:06:14.124
Oooooo-rah!

169
00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:15.709
Um. guys?

170
00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:17.419
My office is this way.
Want to march?

171
00:06:17.502 --> 00:06:19.087
I was just gonna say!

172
00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.714
I don't know
what I've been told!

173
00:06:20.797 --> 00:06:22.591
I've been told
what I've been told!

174
00:06:29.514 --> 00:06:31.141
Spirits! Aliens!

175
00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:32.933
Mutants and Goo-gas!

176
00:06:33.018 --> 00:06:34.978
Welcome to The Triangle!

177
00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.689
You are here because
you have haunted. morphed.

178
00:06:37.772 --> 00:06:40.650
doppelganged. eaten.
or maliciously laid eggs

179
00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:42.986
in the greatest country
on Earth.

180
00:06:43.069 --> 00:06:45.155
Your kingdom
is a fleeting dream.

181
00:06:45.238 --> 00:06:47.407
If death cannot contain me.
how will you?

182
00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:49.326
I am Dracu...

183
00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:52.829
Well. in here.
you are Prisoner 7-5-6-2.

184
00:06:52.913 --> 00:06:55.248
If you open your mouth.
we will shut it.

185
00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:57.542
If you extend a second.
telescoping mouth.

186
00:06:57.626 --> 00:06:59.628
we will teleport you
into solid rock.

187
00:06:59.711 --> 00:07:01.551
I don't want to hear
a single villain monologue

188
00:07:01.588 --> 00:07:04.633
from you worms or a single worm
monologue from you villains.

189
00:07:04.716 --> 00:07:09.346
From here on out. your ass.
ovipositor. pellet tube.

190
00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:12.223
fecal portal.
or possessed car trunk

191
00:07:12.307 --> 00:07:14.351
belongs to me!

192
00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.977
Triangle mint
on a triangle tray?

193
00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:16.895
-Thanks.
-I'm good.

194
00:07:16.978 --> 00:07:19.206
I know what you're thinking...
"That's a pretty pointy shape

195
00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:21.691
to base an entire prison's
interior decor around."

196
00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:24.194
But half of these animals
have razor-sharp bones.

197
00:07:24.277 --> 00:07:26.905
and the other half can suck
your soul through your nostrils.

198
00:07:26.988 --> 00:07:28.990
so why use a plastic
butter knife. right?

199
00:07:29.074 --> 00:07:30.825
I'm mostly worried
about the very large.

200
00:07:30.909 --> 00:07:33.286
triangular trophy displayed
on that remarkably high shelf.

201
00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.246
Ah! You're thinking
if there's a big riot

202
00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.457
and a climactic showdown
in this office.

203
00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.126
I'll end up impaled
by a symbol of my hubris.

204
00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.253
Well. if so.
I'll welcome that death.

205
00:07:42.337 --> 00:07:44.881
Oo-rah!
But also we should talk about

206
00:07:44.965 --> 00:07:46.633
how your prisoners escape a lot.

207
00:07:46.716 --> 00:07:48.385
You're damn right we should.

208
00:07:48.468 --> 00:07:50.762
This prison needs to be
locked down and sealed tight.

209
00:07:50.845 --> 00:07:54.057
I've got a thousand guards.
and I can trust about 50.

210
00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.808
-And they're all marines.
-Marines!

211
00:07:55.892 --> 00:07:57.811
Guys. maybe we could
take a look at the site

212
00:07:57.894 --> 00:07:59.270
of the Loch Ness Monster escape?

213
00:07:59.354 --> 00:08:01.231
I mean. it's just a wall
with a big hole in it.

214
00:08:01.314 --> 00:08:03.274
but if you really think
looking at it will help...

215
00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:05.652
Sorry.
I brought my boss.

216
00:08:09.406 --> 00:08:12.242
Hey. Mister Newbie.
can I ask you a question?

217
00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.911
Are you gonna squeal
like a piggy when I...

218
00:08:14.995 --> 00:08:18.039
rend and mince
the soft puckered flesh

219
00:08:18.123 --> 00:08:20.041
of your sphincter?

220
00:08:20.125 --> 00:08:22.002
Yeah. yeah.
You're a Soul Ganderer.

221
00:08:22.085 --> 00:08:24.462
You can't touch people
that don't look at you.

222
00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.717
He'll try to get you
with a mirror tonight.

223
00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.468
I don't need a prison tutor.

224
00:08:30.552 --> 00:08:31.678
Oh. that's probably true.

225
00:08:31.761 --> 00:08:33.221
You are doing better
than Dracula.

226
00:08:33.304 --> 00:08:35.140
Blah. Blah.

227
00:08:35.222 --> 00:08:36.558
Blah.

228
00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.852
Hey.
Nosfor-cock-tu.

229
00:08:40.311 --> 00:08:41.479
You'll never be cool.

230
00:08:41.563 --> 00:08:42.688
Uh-huh.

231
00:08:46.443 --> 00:08:48.611
Hey. you scanning the room?

232
00:08:48.695 --> 00:08:50.697
It's my job to scan.

233
00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:53.199
He didn't mean any harm.
Metaldetectoid.

234
00:08:53.283 --> 00:08:55.535
If I want any information
from you. I'll scan you.

235
00:08:55.618 --> 00:08:57.579
The only thing
I'm scanning right now

236
00:08:57.662 --> 00:08:59.956
is this half-breed's
triangle jello.

237
00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.416
You should recalibrate.

238
00:09:01.499 --> 00:09:03.209
Ah!
Ah. shit. my lens!

239
00:09:03.293 --> 00:09:05.053
It's pretty crazy
he didn't scan that coming.

240
00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:07.630
Oh. my God.
I-I'm seeing color bars!

241
00:09:07.714 --> 00:09:09.299
This is where Nessie got out.

242
00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:11.092
Triple-plated steel.
Electrified.

243
00:09:11.176 --> 00:09:14.095
Voltage wasn't
Scottish Dinosaur-rated. though.

244
00:09:14.179 --> 00:09:16.181
-That's on me.
-Takes a man to admit that.

245
00:09:16.264 --> 00:09:17.724
What are all these doors?

246
00:09:17.807 --> 00:09:19.476
Part of my new
inmate work initiative.

247
00:09:19.559 --> 00:09:21.186
We have the prisoners
paint the doors.

248
00:09:21.269 --> 00:09:22.687
I got the idea
from "Monsters. Inc."

249
00:09:22.771 --> 00:09:23.605
Huh?

250
00:09:23.688 --> 00:09:25.231
I got a prison
full of monsters. right?

251
00:09:25.315 --> 00:09:26.751
-Why not put 'em to work?
-Right. right.

252
00:09:26.775 --> 00:09:27.984
Like a one-eyed Billy Crystal.

253
00:09:28.068 --> 00:09:30.487
That's what I called
my wiener in the Marines.

254
00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.614
Hey!
Do that thing differently!

255
00:09:32.697 --> 00:09:34.157
Sir. this is getting ridiculous.

256
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:35.760
You've completely dropped
your standards

257
00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:37.094
and are letting this guy
slide on everything

258
00:09:37.118 --> 00:09:38.679
-because he's a Marine.
-That's accurate.

259
00:09:38.703 --> 00:09:40.205
But is that
what a Marine would do?

260
00:09:40.288 --> 00:09:41.873
Nice try.
The answer is yes.

261
00:09:41.956 --> 00:09:44.000
Because the marines are
pre-vetted by the Marines.

262
00:09:44.084 --> 00:09:46.002
If you can be a Marine.
you can do anything.

263
00:09:46.086 --> 00:09:48.254
As long as there's a Pixar movie
to guide you. I guess?

264
00:09:48.338 --> 00:09:50.524
Would it be more rational
for them to make license plates?

265
00:09:50.548 --> 00:09:51.841
Did that trope ever make sense?

266
00:09:51.925 --> 00:09:53.593
He's just making
the place efficient.

267
00:09:53.676 --> 00:09:55.095
Like the Post Office.

268
00:09:55.178 --> 00:09:57.138
Ooh. goddamn.
I love the Post Office.

269
00:09:57.222 --> 00:09:59.307
-Friends. my apologies.
-No problem.

270
00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:00.809
You said you had
a voltage issue?

271
00:10:00.892 --> 00:10:01.952
Should we look at
your power grid?

272
00:10:01.976 --> 00:10:03.436
That is next to the game room.

273
00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:04.771
-Oo-rah!
-Oo-rah!

274
00:10:04.854 --> 00:10:05.854
-Oo-rah!
-Yeah!

275
00:10:05.897 --> 00:10:07.249
I'm just going to
check out some...

276
00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.650
Who cares? You're gone.

277
00:10:10.485 --> 00:10:12.570
Whoa!
Sorry. can't let you do that.

278
00:10:12.654 --> 00:10:14.572
New protocols...
you said no snooping.

279
00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:15.990
Yeah. but I think we just need

280
00:10:16.074 --> 00:10:17.492
to crawl in this hole
and make sure.

281
00:10:17.575 --> 00:10:19.536
Kinda defeats the purpose
of having guidelines.

282
00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.913
You want me to deactivate
so you can do some bad shit?

283
00:10:21.996 --> 00:10:23.540
No. no. I want guidelines.

284
00:10:23.623 --> 00:10:25.041
It's just this once. okay?

285
00:10:25.125 --> 00:10:27.186
If I do it again. you can
double down on the restrictions.

286
00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.587
Sounds like a slippery slope.
but alrighty!

287
00:10:33.967 --> 00:10:35.051
Hey. Those guards...

288
00:10:35.135 --> 00:10:36.946
you think they could help
move some contraband?

289
00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:38.513
Yar! Narc much?

290
00:10:38.596 --> 00:10:40.265
Yar-har-har-har!

291
00:10:40.348 --> 00:10:42.183
He heard a rumor
you're an undercover cop.

292
00:10:42.267 --> 00:10:43.768
Why would anyone think that?

293
00:10:43.852 --> 00:10:45.270
Eh. I can't speak for them.

294
00:10:45.353 --> 00:10:47.814
Me. I've got telepathic
filaments in my tentacles.

295
00:10:47.897 --> 00:10:51.234
so I actually know you're
working for The President.

296
00:10:51.317 --> 00:10:53.403
Hey. relax.
I'm telling you I know

297
00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:55.446
because I want you to find
what you're looking for

298
00:10:55.488 --> 00:10:56.906
before you get killed.

299
00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.825
-And what am I looking for?
-It's not what.

300
00:10:58.908 --> 00:11:00.743
-It's where.
-And where is that?

301
00:11:00.827 --> 00:11:03.580
-Mm. let's just say you're...
-Will you fucking stop?

302
00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:06.708
So-rry! God-uh!

303
00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:09.919
Whoa. whoa. whoa!

304
00:11:10.003 --> 00:11:11.087
Ahh! Ugh!

305
00:11:11.171 --> 00:11:12.213
Ugh! Ugh!

306
00:11:12.297 --> 00:11:13.423
Jesus!

307
00:11:16.551 --> 00:11:18.887
"Prisoner Not Found."
Why am I not surprised?

308
00:11:21.723 --> 00:11:24.058
-Ow! What the hell?
-Hi again!

309
00:11:24.142 --> 00:11:26.537
Looks like you're about to jack
into a dead sentient android.

310
00:11:26.561 --> 00:11:28.897
-That's bad.
-I'm just accessing its memory.

311
00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:30.732
probably to bring its killers
to justice.

312
00:11:30.815 --> 00:11:33.568
But you said to double down
if you broke protocol again.

313
00:11:33.651 --> 00:11:34.651
Oh. my God.

314
00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:37.864
If I do something actually bad.
you can make it hurt.

315
00:11:37.947 --> 00:11:40.533
Until then. override and
give me some damn flexibility.

316
00:11:40.617 --> 00:11:43.620
Don't yell at me.
You programmed me.

317
00:11:43.703 --> 00:11:46.873
Ahhh!
I-I can't take it anymore!

318
00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:48.833
Hernandez. help me
tighten these restraints.

319
00:11:48.917 --> 00:11:51.294
Is it a weird time to say
I'm morally conflicted about this?

320
00:11:51.377 --> 00:11:53.463
No. it's the perfect time.
Hernandez!

321
00:11:53.546 --> 00:11:55.131
Ahhh!

322
00:11:57.592 --> 00:11:59.093
I need to find Hernandez.

323
00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:01.262
Ugh.

324
00:12:01.346 --> 00:12:03.514
Okay.
Side quest completed.

325
00:12:04.474 --> 00:12:05.600
That's it. East Wing.

326
00:12:05.683 --> 00:12:06.935
That's where Nessie went?

327
00:12:07.018 --> 00:12:09.145
Guards tried to take him there.
and he went berserk.

328
00:12:09.229 --> 00:12:11.814
Hell. I don't blame him...
you go there. you never come back.

329
00:12:11.898 --> 00:12:13.441
That's why the escapees

330
00:12:13.524 --> 00:12:15.777
are registered as deceased
before they leave.

331
00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.695
They're not being helped
from inside.

332
00:12:17.779 --> 00:12:20.406
They're being marked for death
and doing their best to get out.

333
00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.116
Yard time is over. freaks!

334
00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.285
Get your ugly asses. carapaces.

335
00:12:24.369 --> 00:12:27.205
and prehensile tails
back inside now!

336
00:12:27.288 --> 00:12:28.915
Not you two.
You know what happens

337
00:12:28.998 --> 00:12:31.209
when inmates try to find out
if we're corrupt. don't ya?

338
00:12:31.292 --> 00:12:32.752
You reveal your corruption?

339
00:12:32.835 --> 00:12:34.128
It's the least we can do.

340
00:12:34.212 --> 00:12:36.381
Hey. Metaldetectoid. you hungry?

341
00:12:36.464 --> 00:12:38.925
Yeah.
For unfinished beef.

342
00:12:39.008 --> 00:12:40.426
How is this a threat?

343
00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:41.820
I already beat this guy up
in one move.

344
00:12:41.844 --> 00:12:43.429
And by scanning that move.

345
00:12:43.513 --> 00:12:46.015
I extrapolated
your entire combat style.

346
00:12:46.099 --> 00:12:48.393
Prepare to fight... yourself!

347
00:12:48.476 --> 00:12:49.686
Rahh!

348
00:12:49.769 --> 00:12:51.312
Ahh!

349
00:12:51.396 --> 00:12:52.689
Why would fighting yourself

350
00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:54.649
be harder than fighting
a stranger?

351
00:12:54.732 --> 00:12:56.734
I fight myself every day!

352
00:12:59.362 --> 00:13:01.072
Hey! Hey!
Whoa. take it easy!

353
00:13:01.155 --> 00:13:03.783
We get it. man! You're good
at kicking your own ass!

354
00:13:03.866 --> 00:13:05.660
You get a pack of cigs
when you kill 'em.

355
00:13:05.743 --> 00:13:07.412
Use your horns.
He's feisty.

356
00:13:07.495 --> 00:13:09.497
If you think
I'm scared of a leprechaun.

357
00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.457
you don't know goat.

358
00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:14.377
You think I'm stupid?

359
00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:16.462
I'm not fighting them
for a pack of cigs!

360
00:13:16.546 --> 00:13:18.923
But I would do it
for a picture of your wife.

361
00:13:19.007 --> 00:13:20.675
Deal.

362
00:13:20.758 --> 00:13:22.635
Mm-mm-mmm.

363
00:13:22.719 --> 00:13:25.763
What's a hot spider like her
even doing with a guy like you?

364
00:13:25.847 --> 00:13:27.223
Maybe it's not really my wife.

365
00:13:27.307 --> 00:13:28.742
Maybe I've been giving you
photos of spiders

366
00:13:28.766 --> 00:13:30.560
to make you do shit.

367
00:13:30.643 --> 00:13:33.062
Tangled in the web
of my own porn addiction.

368
00:13:34.856 --> 00:13:36.441
We're eagle. globe. and anchor

369
00:13:36.524 --> 00:13:37.942
We fight with piss and rancor

370
00:13:38.026 --> 00:13:39.861
Semper Fi. that's my guy

371
00:13:39.944 --> 00:13:41.237
Marines!

372
00:13:41.321 --> 00:13:42.613
Yeah!

373
00:13:42.697 --> 00:13:44.073
It's amazing. isn't it?

374
00:13:44.157 --> 00:13:45.450
We were both soldiers.

375
00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:48.077
and now we're each kings
of our own domains.

376
00:13:48.161 --> 00:13:50.264
In a way. you've got a
harder country to run than I do.

377
00:13:50.288 --> 00:13:52.081
Trying to contain
all these monsters.

378
00:13:52.165 --> 00:13:54.667
Well. if they let me run it
the way I really want.

379
00:13:54.751 --> 00:13:56.210
both of us could be happy.

380
00:13:56.294 --> 00:13:58.713
The world is full
of different folks

381
00:13:58.796 --> 00:14:00.757
And some of them are monsters

382
00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.092
They're not like us.
so lock them up

383
00:14:03.176 --> 00:14:06.220
And seal their screams forever

384
00:14:06.304 --> 00:14:09.349
If the cells get full.
you cull the herd

385
00:14:09.432 --> 00:14:11.142
And their deaths will be my...

386
00:14:11.225 --> 00:14:13.644
Ho! Whoa!
Okay. a little extreme.

387
00:14:13.728 --> 00:14:15.104
I didn't know you'd go
full Nazi.

388
00:14:15.188 --> 00:14:17.648
Aren't people who call
people Nazis the real Nazis?

389
00:14:17.732 --> 00:14:19.859
Nope. Answer your phone.

390
00:14:19.942 --> 00:14:21.235
This is Jeffries.

391
00:14:21.319 --> 00:14:23.446
Christ. Alright. I'm coming.

392
00:14:23.529 --> 00:14:25.073
-What was that?
-Fight in the yard.

393
00:14:25.156 --> 00:14:27.408
A new leprenoid killed
20% of Cell Block D.

394
00:14:27.492 --> 00:14:28.785
Uh. about that.

395
00:14:28.868 --> 00:14:30.328
The "leprenoid's" mine.

396
00:14:30.411 --> 00:14:32.455
Before I came. I. uh...
I put him undercover

397
00:14:32.538 --> 00:14:34.749
because I thought you might
be... incompetent.

398
00:14:34.832 --> 00:14:36.793
Oh.
Quite the "oo-rah" move.

399
00:14:36.876 --> 00:14:38.669
Right?
But you can bring him up here.

400
00:14:38.753 --> 00:14:40.147
He won't be causing you
any more trouble.

401
00:14:40.171 --> 00:14:41.798
You're right about that.

402
00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:42.965
"Guard button?"

403
00:14:43.049 --> 00:14:44.425
Oh. wait... what is this?

404
00:14:44.509 --> 00:14:46.109
I'm sorry it had to come
to this. Curtis.

405
00:14:46.177 --> 00:14:47.470
So really it's a door button.

406
00:14:47.553 --> 00:14:49.281
The guards were already
waiting behind the door.

407
00:14:49.305 --> 00:14:51.158
Also. you really think
you can get away with this?

408
00:14:51.182 --> 00:14:52.308
I'm the President!

409
00:14:52.392 --> 00:14:54.143
You're in the Bermuda Triangle.

410
00:14:54.227 --> 00:14:56.163
It would have been weirder
if you'd made it back home.

411
00:14:56.187 --> 00:14:58.332
Rgh! I guess you pushed the
"bag over the head" button?

412
00:14:58.356 --> 00:14:59.356
Ugh!

413
00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:03.236
Huh?
What is... what is this?

414
00:15:05.488 --> 00:15:07.281
Can't believe
I trusted that monster.

415
00:15:07.365 --> 00:15:09.283
-Not always a bad thing. sir.
-O'Doyle?

416
00:15:09.367 --> 00:15:11.536
I came in here
hating these freaks.

417
00:15:11.619 --> 00:15:14.664
but I found kindness
in a radioactive Swamptopus.

418
00:15:14.747 --> 00:15:15.957
Hi.

419
00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.458
How radioactive is he?

420
00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:19.710
Like a laptop on a crotch or...?

421
00:15:19.794 --> 00:15:21.963
Alright. test subjects
are locked in.

422
00:15:22.046 --> 00:15:23.381
Canisters are online.

423
00:15:23.464 --> 00:15:24.966
Begin the extraction!

424
00:15:25.049 --> 00:15:27.552
Aghh! God in heaven!

425
00:15:29.429 --> 00:15:31.097
Sir. I have a technique
for this...

426
00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.975
Imagine every scream brings
your mother closer to orgasm.

427
00:15:34.058 --> 00:15:36.269
-What?
-So you deprive her of it!

428
00:15:40.731 --> 00:15:42.400
Did the tank fill with anything?

429
00:15:42.483 --> 00:15:44.110
-No. sir.
-Goddammit!

430
00:15:44.193 --> 00:15:46.195
I added microchips
to the canisters.

431
00:15:46.279 --> 00:15:48.739
How is it still not collecting
their screams?

432
00:15:48.823 --> 00:15:50.676
Wait. you're seriously doing
a "Monsters. Inc."?

433
00:15:50.700 --> 00:15:52.118
I told you I was!

434
00:15:52.201 --> 00:15:53.744
You got it backwards. you idiot.

435
00:15:53.828 --> 00:15:55.597
You're supposed
to use children for the screams.

436
00:15:55.621 --> 00:15:57.832
That's what the doors are for!

437
00:15:57.915 --> 00:15:59.584
We were eventually
going to connect them

438
00:15:59.667 --> 00:16:01.294
to children's closets.

439
00:16:01.377 --> 00:16:04.338
And then. of course...
come the giggles.

440
00:16:04.422 --> 00:16:07.216
Goddammit. how desperate was I
to connect with someone?

441
00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:08.843
Check the wiring
and run it again!

442
00:16:08.926 --> 00:16:10.261
Harder!

443
00:16:12.013 --> 00:16:14.432
Hey. pal. this East Wing.
Room 213?

444
00:16:14.515 --> 00:16:16.225
You know it.
Torture central.

445
00:16:16.309 --> 00:16:17.953
You believe that's the
President of the United States

446
00:16:17.977 --> 00:16:19.020
squealing in there?

447
00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:21.720
Thank God.
I don't know how long

448
00:16:21.772 --> 00:16:23.292
I could've sustained
that guard accent.

449
00:16:23.316 --> 00:16:24.525
Urgh!

450
00:16:24.609 --> 00:16:25.818
Oh. shit. shit. shit.

451
00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.365
Ahhh!

452
00:16:31.449 --> 00:16:32.909
What do you think?
Do you like it?

453
00:16:32.992 --> 00:16:34.577
What the fuck?
Why am I on fire?

454
00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.037
I did what you asked!

455
00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:37.840
You're trying to hack
into a federal prison.

456
00:16:37.872 --> 00:16:40.165
Override!
Just open door 213!

457
00:16:40.249 --> 00:16:43.503
Okay. okay.
Hmm. so many doors.

458
00:16:43.586 --> 00:16:45.421
Might take a while to find that.

459
00:16:45.505 --> 00:16:46.839
Hmm. let's see.

460
00:16:46.923 --> 00:16:48.841
Oh. my God.
just open all the doors!

461
00:16:48.925 --> 00:16:50.051
Ahh!
Thought you'd never ask!

462
00:16:50.134 --> 00:16:51.135
I love us. Byeeee!

463
00:16:51.219 --> 00:16:52.261
Ahh!

464
00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:56.933
I'll never do it again!

465
00:16:57.016 --> 00:16:59.393
Ooh! Pain's gone.
Might do it again.

466
00:17:01.938 --> 00:17:03.689
Stop! Let me go!

467
00:17:03.773 --> 00:17:05.398
All I did was lead
a troubled child

468
00:17:05.483 --> 00:17:07.108
to an eternal realm
of light and love!

469
00:17:07.193 --> 00:17:08.319
Never saw it.

470
00:17:09.487 --> 00:17:10.488
Blah!

471
00:17:14.157 --> 00:17:16.493
Yar-ha-ah-ha-har!

472
00:17:20.957 --> 00:17:23.459
Oh shit! Oh. God!
I've been so mean to them!

473
00:17:23.542 --> 00:17:24.669
Oh! Oh. no!

474
00:17:24.752 --> 00:17:25.752
Oh. it's just you.

475
00:17:25.836 --> 00:17:28.005
What are you gonna do.
turn into a bat?

476
00:17:31.342 --> 00:17:33.511
No. no. no. no... agh!

477
00:17:33.594 --> 00:17:35.304
Meeting adjourned.

478
00:17:35.388 --> 00:17:39.433
Check out me. Dracula.
in "Monster Squad." 1987.

479
00:17:39.517 --> 00:17:41.519
What the hell is going on?

480
00:17:43.396 --> 00:17:45.273
Thanks for the lift.
Evil Haunted Car.

481
00:17:45.356 --> 00:17:48.025
I'm not haunted. I'm just evil

482
00:17:48.109 --> 00:17:49.735
You!

483
00:17:49.819 --> 00:17:51.571
It's time to chase you down

484
00:17:51.654 --> 00:17:52.947
Ahh!

485
00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:55.616
Banks!
Holy shit. way to go!

486
00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.060
I know. right?
I'm kind of awesome.

487
00:17:57.118 --> 00:17:58.303
I should've listened to you.
Banks.

488
00:17:58.327 --> 00:18:00.079
I got so sucked up
in Marine culture

489
00:18:00.162 --> 00:18:02.540
and bro-ing out.
I-I took my eyes off the ball.

490
00:18:02.623 --> 00:18:04.500
I was wrong. too. sir.
There's things in here

491
00:18:04.584 --> 00:18:06.085
that need to stay
locked up forever.

492
00:18:06.168 --> 00:18:07.753
Yeah. but not all of them.

493
00:18:07.837 --> 00:18:08.671
Hi.

494
00:18:08.754 --> 00:18:10.798
So. all our lessons
cancel each other out?

495
00:18:10.881 --> 00:18:13.509
Maybe the lesson is that.
together. we learn nothing.

496
00:18:13.593 --> 00:18:15.344
Can we just go back
to that evil car?

497
00:18:15.428 --> 00:18:17.656
I mean. if it was making up
original songs to communicate.

498
00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:19.056
why not just talk?

499
00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:20.600
So much extra work.

500
